  <diagram name="6. Historical Comparison (3/10)" id="UL8_iZpFAf6A71DSmY-2">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1242" dy="-1372" grid="1" gridSize="5" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" background="#CCCCCC" math="0" shadow="0" adaptiveColors="none">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-0" />
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-1" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-0" />
        <UserObject label="Historicity&amp;nbsp;Comparison: Bible vs. Quran (3/10)" link="data:page/id,lkuSvPZcJC7dHRsydWrw" id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-21">
          <mxCell style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#E6E6E6;fontSize=20;" vertex="1" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-1">
            <mxGeometry x="20" y="2225" width="810" height="50" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-50" value="" style="shape=table;startSize=0;container=1;collapsible=0;childLayout=tableLayout;fontSize=1;" vertex="1" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2335" width="810" height="250.00000000000023" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-51" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-50">
          <mxGeometry width="810" height="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-52" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: x-small;&quot;&gt;What are the weakest links in the strongest chains of custodianship?&lt;/b&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#D5D5D5;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;gradientColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-51">
          <mxGeometry width="180" height="250" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="180" height="250" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-53" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;All chains have gaps (either relying on unknown transmission or lost works) except for the Pauline chain&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Synoptic Chains&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Both chains for Mark support the claim that he learned from Peter, but rely on lost work (Papias), an unnamed transmitter, and an unspecified oral tradition.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- The chains for Matthew and Luke both depend on unknown transmitters, and Luke additionally relies on unknown source material.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 8px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Note that both Matthew and Mark state that none of the disciples witnessed the crucifixion (the most important theological event) - meaning that Peter (Mark&#39;s source) wouldn&#39;t have witnessed it either.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Johannine Chain&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- The chain for John depends on Irenaeus, whose claim for John&#39;s authorship relies on Polycarp, who only orally testified this to Irenaeus without writing it in his work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- John is the only one who states that he witnessed the crucifixion.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pauline Chain&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Paul&#39;s letters are self-attesting and corroborated by Clement of Rome.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Ignatius of Antioch also corroborates Paul, but his chain relies on unknown oral transmission.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Jewish Christian&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;/Nazarene&lt;/b&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;, Ebionite, and Gnostic Chains&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- All orthodox-competing chains rely on lost work and unknown oral traditions.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- The Gnostic chain is the exception in that their gospels are preserved, but their chain appears intentionally hidden (according to Irenaeus).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Notes: all chains about the earthly Jesus contain some degree of historical uncertainty.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCFFCC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" vertex="1" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-51">
          <mxGeometry x="180" width="315" height="250" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="250" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-54" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The potential weaknesses of the oral and textual chains are mitigated by the other&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Quranic Chain&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- The standardized written text safeguarded by Hafsah is corroborated by mass memorization, while mass memorization is protected from alteration by the standardized text.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hadith Chain (Sunni)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;The more narrators in a chain, the greater the risk of weakness - especially with single-narrator reports (known as &lt;i&gt;ahad&lt;/i&gt;&amp;nbsp;hadith).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- The science of authenticating hadith and examining narrators was established alongside the compilers, allowing hadith narrations to be classified based on their authenticity - and putting more pressure on the compilers for being reliable.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px; text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hadith Chain (Shia)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Reliability is tied to the infallibility of the narrators, which is unfalsifiable and supported by fewer corroborating chains than in Sunni transmission - leaving greater room for weakness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Notes: the Quran appears to be reliably preserved, while Hadith reliability is dependent on the strength of its compilers and methods.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCE5FF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" vertex="1" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-51">
          <mxGeometry x="495" width="315" height="250" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="250" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-55" value="&lt;b&gt;3. Assessment of the Chains of Transmission (continued)&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#FFF2CC;gradientColor=#FFD966;strokeColor=#D6B656;" vertex="1" parent="oTV51KeiLnIpI_8r1Urz-1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="2290" width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
