    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="6. Historical Comparison (6/10)" id="wSjUeYOFd7Q6O4Wm3PFX">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1242" dy="-4672" grid="1" gridSize="5" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" background="#CCCCCC" math="0" shadow="0" adaptiveColors="none">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-0" />
        <mxCell id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-1" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-0" />
        <UserObject label="Historicity&amp;nbsp;Comparison: Bible vs. Quran (6/10)" link="data:page/id,lkuSvPZcJC7dHRsydWrw" id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-27">
          <mxCell style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#E6E6E6;fontSize=20;" vertex="1" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-1">
            <mxGeometry x="20" y="5525" width="810" height="50" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-83" value="" style="group" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="5590" width="810.0000000000001" height="979.9999999999973" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-84" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;5. Resistance to Fabrication (continued)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#DAE8FC;gradientColor=#7EA6E0;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;" vertex="1" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-83">
          <mxGeometry width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-85" value="" style="shape=table;startSize=0;container=1;collapsible=0;childLayout=tableLayout;fontSize=1;spacingRight=0;" vertex="1" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-83">
          <mxGeometry y="45" width="810" height="934.9999999999973" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-86" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-85">
          <mxGeometry width="810" height="935" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-87" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;How strongly does the claim&#39;s custodianship resist fabrication and error?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;(Requirements for Trusting Defense)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: x-small;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Speculation is not refutation. To be able to distinguish between truth and falsehood, there must be some identifiable property between competing claims that renders one true and the other false.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: x-small;&quot;&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;What is the epistemological difference between reasonable and unreasonable uncertainty?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Acceptance of known constraints: while both assess the uncertainty of a claim, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;reasonable uncertainty respects the strength of their established constraints, while unreasonable uncertainty ignores them - speculating about the unknown instead of reasoning from evidence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;What is the epistemological difference between retroactive assumption and hyperskepticism?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;What is assumed without evidence:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;both appeal to higher-level inference while dismissing the evidence itself, with retroactive assumption accepting truth (without foundational proof) and hyperskepticism rejecting truth (without foundational proof).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#D5D5D5;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;gradientColor=none;spacingRight=2;spacingLeft=2;" vertex="1" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-86">
          <mxGeometry width="180" height="935" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="180" height="935" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-88" value="&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Independently establishing Paul&#39;s reliability and alignment with what the earthly Jesus said (before claiming truth)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The existence of some unknowns doesn&#39;t necessitate unreliability. This is actually very common and expected in oral societies at the time.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;It is true that ancient oral societies commonly preserved information through unknown transmitters, and the mere existence of unknowns does not automatically invalidate a tradition. However, to meaningfully trust these unknowns, we must be able to distinguish between&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;reliable and unreliable unknowns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reliable unknowns&lt;/b&gt;: possible range of outcomes have known constraints&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- &lt;b&gt;Unreliable unknowns&lt;/b&gt;: possible range is open-ended or speculative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Therefore, the real criterion is the reliability of the unknown&#39;s constraints, not cultural commonality.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;The key question is not whether unknowns were common, but whether their outcomes were constrained enough to distinguish truth from falsehood.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Without assessing the constraints of each unknown step, both truth and fabrication remain equally possible, leaving no epistemological difference between them.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;This can be shown by applying the same principle in reverse, as the existence of unknowns doesn&#39;t necessitate reliability either.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Thus, unknowns may not force unreliability - but they do force uncertainty - and accepting them as &quot;good enough&quot; always involves some degree of speculation (as if there is no speculation, then it must be &quot;known&quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The absence of rival texts reflects the success of the early Church in extinguishing false claims.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- This may be true, but n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;o ancient text survives by accident: it survives only because an institution with power, money, and infrastructure continuously copies it for centuries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- As such, for this argument to have substance, t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;his requires that the historical disappearance of rivals be a sign of their falsehood&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;. To verify this, we would need to be able to distinguish between power-based suppression and truth-based suppression:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- &lt;b&gt;Power-based suppression&lt;/b&gt;: when a false institution suppresses truth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- &lt;b&gt;Truth-based suppression&lt;/b&gt;: when a true institution suppresses falsehood&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Therefore,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;the real criterion is first identifying what is true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;(ie. what the earthly Jesus truly said)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;, not retroactively assuming it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;his argument cannot be used before establishing the truth of the claim, or else the logic becomes circular or speculative: &quot;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;hey were wrong because they lost, and they lost because they were wrong&quot;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- This argument also diminishes when the Gospels themselves depict Jesus&#39; victory as spiritual, not a worldly. As such, to be internally consistent, worldly victory does not necessarily indicate spiritual truth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The preserved manuscripts and independent streams corroborate one another.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;T&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;he redundancy from independent origins makes a late, singular fabrication highly improbable.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- It is true that later manuscripts converge and that multiple streams reinforce core events. However,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;this only disproves late fabrication:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;the real window of concern is whether&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;early fabrication (within 1–6 years after the crucifixion) could have occurred before the written Gospels, epistles, and preserved manuscripts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Therefore:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Later manuscript uniformity cannot eliminate the possibility that an early, unified fabrication became dominant. If such an early fabrication occurred and that was the dominant institution, then the preserved manuscripts would necessarily corroborate that same fabrication centuries later - especially if True texts were not preserved.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- To address this possibility, we would need to first compare Jesus&#39; original message to both the claim and the potential fabrication (as both sides claim that he is their source of knowledge), before appealing to manuscript quantity and consistency as a defense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Gospels contain embarrassing details that fabricators wouldn&#39;t intentionally include (as they are trying to win people over), and people willing to die for a claim wouldn&#39;t think that what they believe in is wrong.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Perhaps, but this makes quite a few assumptions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- People have different priorities, and if people lie in order to gain in some way (that being honest doesn&#39;t), then they will maintain that lie so long as they&#39;re accomplishing their goal. As such, this argument assumes that a fabricator can&#39;t gain anything by weakening their argument or using embarrassing details.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- This also assumes that 1st century fabricators couldn&#39;t have been clever enough to know this, and use it to their advantage. Moreover, a fabricator may have included an embarrassing detail to fit within their narrative, or to perhaps hide a more embarrassing event that would be damaging to their fabrication.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Therefore, the defense&#39;s strength depends on the belief that such clever fabrication is psychologically improbable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Therefore:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;While the embarrassment criterion can indeed support authenticity, it is not strong enough on its own to eliminate the possibility of deliberate fabrication without further investigation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Differing Christologies don&#39;t contradict each other and reflect progressive revelation, not gradual development.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Both appeal to the same sources and involve incremental additions:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- &lt;b&gt;Progressive revelation&lt;/b&gt;: gradually reveals a new part of the whole Truth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- &lt;b&gt;Gradual development&lt;/b&gt;: gradually reveals a new part of a developing falsehood&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Therefore,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;the real criterion is first identifying what is true (ie. what the earthly Jesus truly said), not retroactively assuming it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Progressive revelation cannot function as proof; it assumes the very thing it is trying to prove.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- If this argument is valid, then we can use the same data and logic to make the opposite claim (ie. differing Christologies show gradual development, not progressive revelation).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Without first assessing whether the claims align with what Jesus himself said, then both sides equally fit the data (ie. truth is indistinguishable from falsehood).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- This means that this argument&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;can only be persuasive after establishing that the earthly Jesus himself said. Otherwise, using it first would be&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;circular reasoning: &quot;it&#39;s progressive revelation because it&#39;s true, and its truth is reflected in its progressive revelation&quot;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- P&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; text-align: center; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;aul&#39;s authority is the strongest proof of the gospel&#39;s divine origin.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- If the claim&#39;s truth rests heavily on the truth of Paul&#39;s post-resurrection vision, then Paul first needs to be established as a reliable source of information. As such, he needs to be assessed under the same standards that we did with Jesus - meaning the elimination of him being a liar, lunatic, or demonically influenced.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCFFCC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-86">
          <mxGeometry x="180" width="315" height="935" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="935" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-89" value="&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Eliminating all plausible natural pathways for fabrication or alteration&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- The Quran was revealed during Muhammad&#39;s lifetime.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;The Quran indeed references historical events, shared disputes, and unfolding situations that clearly fit within a 7th-century Arabian context. However, a text that references a historical setting is not necessarily a text that originated in that setting. As such, we must distinguish between primary and secondary sources:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- &lt;b&gt;Primary source&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;: a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;text produced by eyewitnesses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;Secondary source&lt;/b&gt;: a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;text produced by non-eyewitnesses, whose sources are eyewitness accounts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- Therefore, the key criterion is identifying if the Quran contains information that only a primary eyewitnesses could have known.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;As such, t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;o trust the claim, the argument must show the presence of historically inaccessible details: information that could not be retroactively recovered or engineered by a later source.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); font-size: 2px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Muhammad is the only possible candidate for the Quran&#39;s revelation.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- It is true that there is a strong, historical case for Muhammad orally transmitting the Quran, but his illiteracy and documented incapacity to produce such a sophisticated work makes it difficult to attribute him as the source - without appealing to a divine cause, as the Quran itself argues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- As a result, for this argument to have substance, it requires the elimination of natural explanations for the Quran&#39;s authorship, which reduces to the elimination alternative authors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;The analysis must show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;the established historical conditions of 7th-century Arabia could not have allowed the Quran to be produced, compiled, or shaped through hidden individuals or distributed networks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Therefore, the real criterion is whether the historical conditions make alternative authorship impossible, rather than merely unrecorded. The analysis must show:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- &lt;b&gt;No individual alternative&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;no educated poet, scribe, monk, scholar, or informant possessed the combined linguistic, theological, and structural capacity to engineer a text of this scope and coherence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- &lt;b&gt;No collaborative alternative&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;no political faction, tribal network, or scribal institution had both the capability and secrecy to produce (or coordinate) the Quran without contradiction, infiltration, exposure, or competing claims&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;- &lt;b&gt;Internal consistency&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;no internal evidence of layered composition, stylistic plurality, editorial seams, or revision-patterns that would indicate distributed authorship, literary construction, or developmental redaction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Only when these natural explanations are excluded by constraint - not simply absent from record - can the argument stand as a justified historical conclusion.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Quran&#39;s text was reliably preserved without alteration.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Public recitation, widespread memorization, and early manuscript activity indeed provide substantial evidence for preservation. However, if the Quran&#39;s preservation is attributed to divine intervention - as the text itself claims - then the historical defense necessitates the elimination of alternative explanations within the established historical constraints&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237));&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Therefore, the real criterion is&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;whether the Quran&#39;s transmission environment closed every window of potential corruption before standardization. The analysis must show that:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;No monopolization&lt;/b&gt;: no early caliphate, scribal authority, or regional leader ever had exclusive control of the text long enough to modify it before public re-diffusion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;No collaborative alternative&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;no political faction, tribal network, or scribal institution had both the capability and secrecy to produce (or coordinate) the Quran without contradiction, infiltration, exposure, or competing claims&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;Internal consistency&lt;/b&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;no internal evidence of layered composition, stylistic plurality, editorial seams, or revision-patterns that would indicate distributed authorship, literary construction, or developmental redaction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(237, 237, 237)); background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Only when these corruption windows are positively ruled out - not merely unrecorded - does the preservation claim move from probable to historically secure.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Note that&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;each requirement ultimately reduces to the elimination of plausible alternatives - in the absence of documented alternatives. This reflects the distinction between &lt;b&gt;reasonable uncertainty&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;speculative doubt &lt;/b&gt;(or, &lt;b&gt;unreasonable uncertainty&lt;/b&gt;): the mere absence of rival narratives does not by itself prove exclusivity (since &quot;absence of evidence is not evidence of absence&quot;), but if a text originated publicly, was preserved from the outset, and faced no viable conditions for alternative versions to develop, then the absence of rivals is exactly what we would expect. Once a claim&#39;s environment leaves no plausible pathway for an alternative, demanding imaginary alternatives becomes speculation, not skepticism (since &quot;speculation is not refutation&quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;This guards against both &lt;b&gt;retroactive assumption&lt;/b&gt; (accepting a claim merely because no rival is recorded) and &lt;b&gt;hyperskepticism&lt;/b&gt; (rejecting a claim by inventing scenarios without evidence). Instead, we commit to evidence-based constraints applied to known history, ensuring that our conclusions rest on what is possible under the documented environment, not on blind trust or imaginative doubt.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCE5FF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" vertex="1" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-86">
          <mxGeometry x="495" width="315" height="935" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="935" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="" link="data:page/id,Qv_htXwKxnLwx0oGmtAl" id="cDfrxOZJRTFbDFn1Vne--0">
          <mxCell style="group;rotation=-180;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="bwPMnbwdrdVlshME2wuY-1">
            <mxGeometry x="780" y="5525" width="50" height="50" as="geometry" />
