  <diagram name="6. Historical Comparison (10/10)" id="lD0beqhCFwfZuSMG6im9">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1242" dy="-9072" grid="1" gridSize="5" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" background="#CCCCCC" math="0" shadow="0" adaptiveColors="none">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-0" />
        <mxCell id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-1" parent="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-0" />
        <UserObject label="Historicity&amp;nbsp;Comparison: Bible vs. Quran (10/10)" link="data:page/id,lkuSvPZcJC7dHRsydWrw" id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-82">
          <mxCell style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#E6E6E6;fontSize=20;" vertex="1" parent="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-1">
            <mxGeometry x="20" y="9925" width="810" height="50" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="fmysGeRlq7T1k-986xeI-1" value="" style="group" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="9990" width="810.0000000000001" height="1000" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-75" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;7. Conclusion&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#E6D0DE;gradientColor=#D5739D;strokeColor=#996185;" vertex="1" parent="fmysGeRlq7T1k-986xeI-1">
          <mxGeometry width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-76" value="" style="shape=table;startSize=0;container=1;collapsible=0;childLayout=tableLayout;fontSize=1;spacingBottom=0;" vertex="1" parent="fmysGeRlq7T1k-986xeI-1">
          <mxGeometry y="45" width="810" height="955" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-77" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-76">
          <mxGeometry width="810" height="955" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-78" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;How strong is the claim and its custodianship?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=#666666;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#D5D5D5;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;gradientColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-77">
          <mxGeometry width="180" height="955" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="180" height="955" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-79" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Weak claim, moderate custodianship, all defenses requiring retroactive assumptions of truth&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 4px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Although the Gospels portray a Jesus whose character strongly resists the charge of fabrication, the reliability of his message solely depends on the integrity of its transmission. Because Jesus left no verified writings and authorized no surviving text during his lifetime, all information about him reached us through later custodians. This means that if fabrication or error occurred, it must have entered through the channels that preserved his memory - not through Jesus himself. T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;he establishment of the truth, therefore, shifts to them.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;In the earliest period, those channels were not unified. Multiple teachers, communities, and gospels circulated in competition with one another. Among these, the stream that prevailed and became mainstream Christianity was the Pauline stream. Paul&#39;s letters are the earliest surviving Christian writings, and his theology most closely resembles later Trinitarian orthodoxy. However, the New Testament itself records that Paul faced persistent accusations from other early Christians, and several of his practices - most notably his stance on the Law - sharply diverged from the Jewish followers of Jesus. When these criticisms are read alongside Jesus&#39; own warnings about false teachers, the result is not proof that Paul was unreliable, but that reasonable doubt cannot be eliminated.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;To defend Paul as the authoritative transmitter of Jesus&#39; message, one must either retroactively assume that his version was divinely protected, or appeal to the strength of the early Church&#39;s custodianship to dismiss the possibility of early theological corruption.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;Yet when examining the Gospel tradition, the same pattern appears. All 4 Gospels were written after Paul&#39;s letters. Only 2 are attributed to eyewitnesses, and only one is claimed to have witnessed the crucifixion itself, the single most important event in Christian theology. Yet John is also the latest Gospel and reflects the highest Christology, written after decades of doctrinal development and corresponding at a time when Pauline Christianity had already gained traction. Meanwhile, the chains of transmission that lead to these texts pass through a long period of lost sources, anonymous editors, and unknown oral transmitters. The first figure to clearly name the four Gospels as a unified canon is Irenaeus, writing roughly 150 years after Jesus. His testimony is also self-referential: we possess no independent corroboration for his claims (that don&#39;t appeal to unknown transmission), nor for his descriptions of the rival Christian groups whose writings have vanished. Thus, all surviving transmission streams - including the winning one - rest on broken links, lost documents, and insiders attesting to themselves.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;As a result, the reliability of the New Testament cannot be established without speculation or retroactive assumption. It&#39;s a double-edged sword: dating the Gospels earlier shortens the writing gap but lengthens the period of untraceable oral transmission; dating them later shortens the oral period but places composition farther from the events. Either way, unknown transmission is unavoidable. Because “all information requires a source” and claims must be externally verifiable to distinguish them from fabrication, a system whose core doctrines rely on untestable links and self-attestation appears to fundamentally act just like a false claim - producing a fatal circular dependency: the doctrine is needed to trust the text, but the text is needed to justify the doctrine. It is an infinite regress of trustworthiness: both depend on the other&#39;s reliability, yet neither can function as the independent foundation for the other - thus contradicting &quot;all information has a source&quot;. A truth claim that cannot stand without first being assumed collapses under its own epistemology - it can&#39;t be called&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;“trustworthy” if the defense relies on assumptions that themselves still require proof.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;This leads to the same result reached in the previous section: Trinitarianism cannot ground its core belief - God&#39;s nature - in either a self-consistent logical model, or a historically verifiable transmission. The failure of one magnifies the weakness of the other. If the theology is false, the historical weakness is expected; if the theology is true, its preservation should be clear, consistent, and resistant to fabrication from the start. This is not what the Biblical historical record reflects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCFFCC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingLeft=1;spacingTop=0;" vertex="1" parent="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-77">
          <mxGeometry x="180" width="315" height="955" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="955" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-80" value="&lt;font size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Strong claim (pending logical verification), strong custodianship, alternatives require historically unsupported speculation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 4px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;The Quran claims to be the direct speech of God, revealed in Arabic through Muhammad over 23 years, recited publicly in specific historical moments, memorized verbatim by many contemporaries, and written down by named scribes while he was alive. Within about two years of his death it was compiled as a complete written corpus, then pronunciation/diacritics were standardized within two decades (to prevent drift as Islam expanded to non-Arabic regions). We still have very early manuscript evidence and a continuous oral tradition consistent with that corpus, and no rival claims to the Quran&#39;s authorship is ever recorded as a sustained, competing lineage. The result is an unusually redundant chain (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;oral plus written, public plus named individuals) that sharply limits the space for silent post-Muhammad alteration.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;As a result, because that custodianship is so constrained, any serious challenge has to be aimed at Muhammad himself. The options are: (1) he knowingly fabricated it, (2) he was deluded, (3) he was influenced by a deceptive supernatural source, or (4) he absorbed and repackaged outside material (from Jews, Christians, poets, storytellers) using extraordinary native brilliance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;The first option (conscious fabrication) sits badly with cost and timing. Muhammad delivered material that attacked his society&#39;s religious authority and economics while he and his followers were weak, targeted, and in danger. He refused offers of wealth and status to stop. He also recited verses that restricted him personally, publicly corrected him, or created short-term exposure in return for long-term outcomes that, at the time, did not look realistic to expect. This is not how a self-serving fabricator normally behaves, because it trades immediate safety for futures that were not obviously achievable when spoken.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;The second option (delusion/instability) is hard to reconcile with the historical result: over those same 23 years, he is credited with unifying rival tribes under a shared moral-legal order, institutionalizing daily communal recitation of the text, and leaving behind a movement that heavily tied itself to both his personality and the text itself (leading to a golden age at a time of global darkness). That pattern looks like disciplined social and intellectual structuring, not incoherence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;The third option (demonic influence) runs into self-sabotage. The Quran repeatedly teaches listeners to seek refuge in God from satanic manipulation, gives criteria for detecting deception, and portrays demonic influence as an enemy to be unmasked and resisted. That is not how a deceiver typically sustains control; it arms the audience against the deceiver&#39;s own alleged method.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;The fourth option says: Muhammad was simply astonishing - a kind of untrained prodigy who absorbed Jewish, Christian, and regional ideas, reorganized them into a single totalizing theology, expressed them in highly structured, high-register Arabic that impressed expert audiences, and then delivered that material live, on demand, across decades, without visible drafting, revision, or collapse of internal stance - all while running a community, negotiating tribal politics, surviving persecution, and leading in war. This explanation requires assuming an unprecedented combination of flawless memory, literary invention, theological synthesis, political foresight, and timing luck - all appearing in a man with no prior record of producing anything like this before prophethood and under severe, hostile scrutiny once it began. That level of &quot;coincidental brilliance plus perfect execution&quot; is not historically nor logically defensible, as invoking it is itself a speculative assumption that goes beyond the observable record.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;What remains after those routes is this: the main exposure point is Muhammad himself, not later editors. The transmission after him is so tightly constrained and publicly checkable that there is no parallel Quranic lineage to appeal to. The next question, then, is not further speculation in &quot;was the Quran altered?&quot; but &quot;is the Quran what it says it is?&quot; The Quran claims to be the direct speech of God. On its own terms, that means it must be internally self-consistent, free of contradiction, and aligned with sound reasoning and observable reality, because it ties God to perfect truth and non-contradiction. This is addressed in the following analysis, which tests to verify that claim of internal and external coherence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CBE2FF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingLeft=1;spacingTop=0;" vertex="1" parent="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-77">
          <mxGeometry x="495" width="315" height="955" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="315" height="955" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-112" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;If truth is defined by consistency, and God is the Truth, and reality itself is sustained by His consistent and unwavering will, then the true religion (by definition) must reflect that same, maximal consistency in both its message and its preservation. As a result, a belief that must be presupposed or speculated about in order to be defended can&#39;t be verified or be distinguishable from falsehood - and a system that cannot distinguish itself from a well-crafted falsehood cannot serve as a reliable guide to ultimate truth. And when we apply that to the New Testament and Quran, we find that the direction of speculation flips: &lt;b&gt;the preservation of the New Testament requires speculation to be true&lt;/b&gt;, while &lt;b&gt;the preservation of the Quran requires speculation to be false&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 7px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;For the New Testament, the central claim (that Jesus is divine in the Trinitarian sense) passes through transmission lines with anonymous or lost intermediaries, early competing claims (to which their works and arguments are lost), and later standardization. In order to beliive that this theology is true (ie. is the original), we have to first assume that the winning stream preserved the authentic truth, that rising Christology is &quot;progressive revelation&quot; and not doctrinal evolution, and that rivals were mistaken. But this is self-referential: the doctrine is used to validate the text, and the text is used to validate the doctrine: the claim needs speculation to prove that it is true.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 7px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;For the Quran, the core claim (that it is the direct speech of God) is tied to established historical constraints: Muhammad publicly recited it in real time, eyewitnesses mass-memorized the text verbatim, known scribes wrote while he was alive, it was compiled within two years of his death, and its pronunciation was stabilized across the community within two decades. Early manuscript evidence and established 7th century Arab standards corroborate these constraints, and no rival claims to the Quran&#39;s transmission exist (neither before nor after Muhammad&#39;s death). That means the usual path for post-founder corruption (quiet or hidden revision, doctrinal editing generations later) is largely blocked. To reject authenticity, you can&#39;t point to a vague gap in transmission; you&#39;d have to argue that Muhammad himself fabricated the Quran or was otherwise the single point of failure - but this also conflicts with the historical constraints. In other words, here the speculation runs the other way: the Quran needs speculation to be false.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 7px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;In comparison with the New Testament, the Quran enters history with a different pattern of preservation - public, continuous, and empirically accessible - making fabrication difficult from the start. If we judged the Quran by the Bible&#39;s standards, it would exceed what Muslims even claim for it; and if we judged the Bible by the Quran&#39;s standards, it would be considered one of the weakest narrations. The Quran&#39;s defenses are also stronger manifestations of the same categories: a “living tradition” is where the entire community safeguards the text, with any normal person being able to correct an authority (not the expectation of differing accounts); &quot;progressive revelation&quot; is where it was revealed over time while the Messenger is still alive and held accountable in public (not where fundamental narratives are written decades after his death); and &quot;God preserved the scripture&quot; is where preservation is obvious to a normal while incapacitating the plausibility of alternatives (not&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;where it requires speculation to do the same&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;). This also makes verification accessible: it is communal and open, not dependent on specialists. By contrast, defending the New Testament&#39;s highest claims requires expert historical reconstruction to decide which sources are &quot;authentic&quot;, why rivals are invalid, and why one theological line alone goes back to Jesus without modification.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;This raises a basic question: if revelation is meant to guide both the uneducated and the elite, why would salvation depend on arguments and knowledge that ordinary people can&#39;t personally verify?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 7px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;All of this lands us in the same place: a belief that must be presupposed in order to be defended cannot be independently verified or meaningfully distinguished from a well-crafted falsehood. And a system whose historical record is objectively weaker than that of a rival claim cannot be the final revelation of the God who authored reality, because the true religion cannot be less &quot;true&quot; - less consistent, less constrained against fabrication, less available to honest scrutiny - than a false one.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 7px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;From here, the question shifts. The Quran does not only claim preservation; it claims to be the direct speech of God and the epitome of consistency - even inviting readers to test its claims. As such, the next section compares the &quot;fruits&quot; of Christianity with Islam&#39;s - verifying its inimitable internal coherence, moral structure, and correspondence with reality.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;gradientColor=#CBE2FF;fillColor=#CCFFCC;gradientDirection=east;fontSize=1;" vertex="1" parent="fmysGeRlq7T1k-986xeI-1">
          <mxGeometry x="180" y="670" width="630" height="330" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="" link="data:page/id,PScHr4ANaqiKAfRTAOgF" id="ihz7weS6olrQnlx0yEaq-3">
          <mxCell style="group;rotation=0;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="cJVLKbOjtSgQkCSZX08d-1">
            <mxGeometry x="20" y="9925" width="50" height="50" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" id="ihz7weS6olrQnlx0yEaq-4">
          <mxCell style="shape=flexArrow;endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fillColor=#B3B3B3;" edge="1" parent="ihz7weS6olrQnlx0yEaq-3">
            <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
              <mxPoint x="50" y="25" as="sourcePoint" />
              <mxPoint x="10" y="25" as="targetPoint" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="ihz7weS6olrQnlx0yEaq-5" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;pointerEvents=0;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=default;fillColor=none;gradientColor=none;strokeColor=none;rotation=0;" vertex="1" parent="ihz7weS6olrQnlx0yEaq-3">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="7. Non-Fundamental Comparison" id="XbJ0z0nIzhYvPX_4MN__">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1213" dy="-9072" grid="1" gridSize="5" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" background="#CCCCCC" math="0" shadow="0" adaptiveColors="none">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-0" />
        <mxCell id="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-0" />
        <UserObject label="Non-Fundamental Comparison: Christianity vs. Islam" link="data:page/id,lkuSvPZcJC7dHRsydWrw" id="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-2">
          <mxCell style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#E6E6E6;fontSize=20;" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry x="20" y="9925" width="810" height="50" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="X1ds6PABbdby7qqjh38H-14" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;1. What is the relationship between God&#39;s mercy/love, justice, and forgiveness (soteriology)?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#f8cecc;gradientColor=#ea6b66;strokeColor=#b85450;" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="9995" width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Lf1yWK0Lw0H-mV7IPuVQ-0" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;2. What is the source of the fundamental, theological difference in soteriology?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#FFDEC9;gradientColor=#FFB663;strokeColor=#D69555;" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="10355" width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Fk_qG9YGPnuzH20UbjZS-0" value="&lt;b&gt;3. Which salvific narrative better fits reality?&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#FFF2CC;gradientColor=#FFD966;strokeColor=#D6B656;" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="10430" width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="EYc5J0ixb2I8HEf8Tvmf-0" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;4. How well do the scriptures&#39; objective properties fit their internal claims?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#D5E8D4;gradientColor=#97D077;strokeColor=#82B366;" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="10505" width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="SICcQmrAYQ4tHytVPw1F-0" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;5. Does anything stand out from the organized religions?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#DAE8FC;gradientColor=#7EA6E0;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="25" y="10580" width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="Jj9n675K-Z2j2yZQ0L7o-0" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;6. Are these results internally consistent with previous conclusions?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#DCDBFC;gradientColor=#9393E0;strokeColor=#8381BF;" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="25" y="10650" width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="PJfseEPP3wY5v_qOuSvO-0" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font&gt;7. Conclusion&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=18;fillColor=#E6D0DE;gradientColor=#D5739D;strokeColor=#996185;" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="25" y="10720" width="810.0000000000001" height="44.9999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdP4uL2IWqcHji0CoqKW-13" value="" style="shape=table;startSize=0;container=1;collapsible=0;childLayout=tableLayout;fontSize=1;" parent="0ffwS5z20CiL1abtpJwu-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="10040" width="810" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdP4uL2IWqcHji0CoqKW-14" value="" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" parent="fdP4uL2IWqcHji0CoqKW-13" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry width="810" height="205" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdP4uL2IWqcHji0CoqKW-16" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 9px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Forgiveness is possible because justice is satisfied by Jesus satisfying the debt of humanity&#39;s sin out of God&#39;s love for us&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Justice&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Giving everyone what they deserve (ie. what they have a right to experience, based on how well they fulfilled their responsibilities).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- More specifically, the debt of sin must be satisfied with a punishment - proportional to the sin&#39;s weight.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Forgiveness&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- When the punishment for a sin is removed.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- This can only occur &lt;i&gt;after&lt;/i&gt; the debt is satisfied (ie. the punishment is experienced) - either when the offender experiences it himself, or if someone else willingly intercedes and experiences it on their behalf.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 2px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Love/Mercy&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- God is love itself: the very essence of affectionately desiring our salvation and happiness.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;- This is ultimately manifested in the Atonement, in which Jesus (the filiation - Person of the Son) satisfied humanity&#39;s debt through his resurrection (by defeating death - the ultimate result of Adam and Eve&#39;s original sin) - changing the fundamental salvific requirement from &quot;impossibily perfect righteousness and repentance&quot; to &quot;faith in Jesus Christ&quot; (ie. belief in his divinity).&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 8px;&quot;&gt;God&#39;s forgiveness of our sins is only possible because justice is still being satisfied by means of the Atonement - saving us from the impossible debt of our own sins.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCFFCC;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" parent="fdP4uL2IWqcHji0CoqKW-14" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry width="405" height="205" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="405" height="205" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fdP4uL2IWqcHji0CoqKW-17" value="" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#CCE5FF;top=1;left=1;bottom=1;right=1;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=1;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;spacingLeft=1;spacingRight=1;spacingBottom=0;spacingTop=-2;" parent="fdP4uL2IWqcHji0CoqKW-14" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="405" width="405" height="205" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="405" height="205" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="6EO3iycbL_vFDhKmOSQg-0" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" parent="fdP4uL2IWqcHji0CoqKW-13" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry y="205" width="810" height="95" as="geometry" />
